is, a new list where the ith element is the sum of the first i + 1 elements from the original list. For
example, the cumulative sum of [1, 2, 3] is [1, 3, 6]."""
def cumulative_sum(array: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float] {
    res = [];
    val = 0;
    for elem in array {
        val += elem;
        res.append(val);
    }
    return res;
}

